        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758493,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The PlayStation 2 (PS2) is a sixth-generation home video game console developed and marketed by Sony Computer Entertainment, released in Japan on March 4, 2000. It succeeded the original PlayStation and remains the best-selling video game console of all time, with over 160 million units sold worldwide. A key innovation was its integrated DVD drive, offering significant value compared to standalone players. \n\nThe PS2 boasted a custom-built Emotion Engine processor, delivering impressive graphics and performance, and was backward compatible with original PlayStation games. Popular titles include the *Grand Theft Auto*, *Final Fantasy*, *Silent Hill*, and *Metal Gear* series, alongside beloved exclusives like *God of War*, *Ratchet & Clank*, and *Jak and Daxter*. Its longevity was remarkable, with new games released until 2013, solidifying its place in gaming history."
          },
